    "hypothesis": "A reusable bottom-up merge sort should eliminate the dominant quadratic column-sorting cost; fusing the two mean traversals and the post-sort statistics scan may further reduce memory passes without changing each metric’s accumulation order. Avoiding OpenMP also avoids the overhead seen in the archived timings.",
    "notes": "NaN-containing columns retain bubble-sort ordering and use the original global-count mode scan with initialized local counts. Finite columns use stable sorting and a run scan that preserves first-tie behavior and the original float mode/count conversions. Parallel variants were not retained because their archived end-to-end times were slower.",
